  "title": "Hardening the Registers: A Cascading Failure of Edge Induced Fault Tolerance",
  "summary": "An article by John Engelman : In 2017, Target announced that we had prioritized stores at the center of how we serve our guests – no matter how they choose to shop. To make this store-as-hubs model work, we spent several years redesigning operations and modernizing how we conduct business. We invested billions of dollars into remodeling stores, hardened our world-class supply chain, and created a robust suite of fulfillment options to meet every guest need.",
